# Database Schema Guidelines

## Database

- PostgreSQL

## Principles

- Normalize data
- Maintain referential integrity
- Design for analytics

## Naming Conventions

- snake_case for tables and columns
- plural table names

## Relationships

- transactions -> categories
- transactions -> accounts
- debts -> accounts
- investments -> accounts

## Time-Series Strategy

- Always store timestamps
- Never overwrite historical data
- Prefer append-only patterns

## Constraints

- Foreign keys required
- Avoid nullable critical fields
- Use indexes for performance

## Performance

- Index date fields
- Index foreign keys
- Use aggregation queries for reports
